      "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Identity-preserving model sheet correction. Use exact Brambleguard from input: bark/root thick limbs, graystone armor/moss/leaf twigs, blue diamond chest core. Render EXACTLY FOUR full-body views in four equal horizontal cells on wide landscape canvas. FRONT, RIGHT PROFILE, BACK, THREEQUARTER RIGHT, chronological left to right. CRITICAL: scale EACH creature much smaller so creature height is only 60 percent canvas height and width max 65percent its own quarter-cell. Ample clear TRANSPARENT gutters between every view; margins at least 50px each side of every character. Current model too large/crowded; fix spacing, don't cut any fist or branch. Uniform scale all four. Preserve hand-painted outline style and design. No ground, cast shadow, haze, text, labels, borders, panels or other chars. Genuine transparent background and opaque interiors. Blue core stays blue, back has no core.",
